---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageBanner from '../../components/PageBanner.astro';

const title = 'Testing Service Policy — Sanshi Bio';
const description = 'Sanshi Bio testing service policy: sample acceptance, rejection, turnaround, reports, re-testing, refunds, retention and report use.';
const breadcrumbLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://sanshibio.net/en/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Testing Service Policy' },
  ],
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd]}>
  <PageBanner title="Testing Service Policy" description="Check sample, turnaround, re-test and report-use rules before submission" breadcrumb="Testing Service Policy" />

  <section class="container-site py-16">
    <div class="prose-sanshi mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500"><em>Last updated: 2026-11-24</em></p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy explains the operational boundaries of Sanshi Bio testing services: racing-pigeon
        gene testing, pathogen testing, paternity testing, sex identification and related technical
        services. Price, sample requirements, turnaround and report format are set by the quotation,
        order or written confirmation. This policy does not replace the
        <a href="/en/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a> and is not a veterinary diagnosis or a
        guarantee of race performance.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">2. Sample acceptance and rejection</h2>
      <p>
        On receipt, the laboratory checks sample type, quantity, packaging, labelling and condition.
        A sample may be rejected or re-sampling requested where:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>the sample is insufficient, degraded, contaminated or improperly stored/shipped;</li>
        <li>the bird ID, ring number or sample ID does not match or the label is unreadable;</li>
        <li>the sample type does not match the test;</li>
        <li>required client information, payment or authorisation is missing;</li>
        <li>an undisclosed biosafety risk is present.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Rejection is a quality-control decision, not a judgement about the client. Re-sampling,
        re-testing or delay caused by a sample issue follows the order terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">3. Turnaround and reports</h2>
      <p>
        Turnaround starts when a suitable sample is received and confirmed, and excludes transport,
        payment, re-sampling, re-testing, holidays or force majeure. Reports are normally delivered
        electronically; paper or other formats must be agreed in advance. A report applies to the
        received sample and is limited by sampling time, sample quality, pathogen load and the test
        method.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">4. Re-testing, cancellation and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        If you question a result, contact us promptly with the sample ID, test and specific concern.
        Whether a re-test is possible, whether a new sample is needed and whether a fee applies depends
        on the remaining sample, the test type and the order terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cancellation before testing begins follows the order terms. If a sample has been received,
        processed or testing has begun, costs already incurred may apply. A failure caused by the
        laboratory is handled by a re-test or refund as agreed in the order; a failure caused by
        sample quality, incorrect information, client action or force majeure is not a laboratory
        breach. Specific refund and liability terms are governed by the written order and applicable
        law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">5. Samples, data and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Samples and test data are used only to perform the requested test, support re-testing, keep
        quality records and communicate about the service. Retention, destruction, re-test use and the
        involvement of third-party laboratories or service providers follow the project, order and
        applicable law. We do not use samples or reports for unrelated purposes or disclose them to
        unrelated third parties.
      </p>
      <p>
        Personal information is handled under the <a href="/en/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        To access, correct or delete personal information, or to request sample handling, use the
        <a href="/en/contact">contact page</a>, subject to legal or quality-record retention
        requirements.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">6. Report-use boundaries</h2>
      <p>
        Reports are for the client or a written authorised recipient, for lawful breeding, health
        management, transaction verification or registration. Do not forge, alter, misquote or use a
        report to mislead a counterparty. Gene testing describes probability and direction; it does
        not guarantee race results, breeding outcomes or transaction value. Pathogen results must be
        interpreted with clinical signs, epidemiology, re-testing and veterinary advice.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">7. Contact and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this policy, samples, reports or complaints, use the
        <a href="/en/contact">contact page</a> or email
        <a href="mailto:martin@senobiocorp.com">martin@senobiocorp.com</a>. Related pages:
        <a href="/en/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>,
        <a href="/en/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>,
        <a href="/en/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
